  "body": "Currently, the Request constructor always resets the request `origin` internal field to \"client\".  See step 12 in:\r\n\r\nhttps://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-request\r\n\r\nThis is problematic because a pass-through FetchEvent SW handler will end up using the service worker's origin for things like:\r\n\r\n* Origin header\r\n* Sec-Fetch-Site header\r\n* SameSite cookies\r\n\r\nIt would be safer for sites if we propagated the internal `origin` field from the original request.  We also need to propagate the `tainted origin flag` as well in order to properly handle redirects.\r\n\r\nThis was discussed at the virtual F2F (w3c/ServiceWorker#1604).  [Notes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q74ATke1oG2jEval1yBTVIrXZGItFi6DR5l8n_8ybgs/edit#bookmark=id.bg7ds8878foi) are available.",
